ract while learning how the rest of the world lives. Financial Aid 2013-2014 Forms 2012-2013 Forms Distribution of Aid Grants Scholarships Work Study Loans Satisfactory Academic Progress Veterans Study Abroad Aid Refund Policy Special Circumstances Financial Aid Application Steps Step 1 Apply for Admittance to Southwestern Acceptance to the university is required before a student can be awarded federal or state aid. To check your acceptance status, you may contact the Admissions Office at (800) 645-3921 ext. 6733. Step 2 Complete the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA). Request a PIN # at the Federal Student Aid PIN Web site . (Student and parents use PIN numbers as an electronic signature on the FAFSA) Complete an application: Online at the Federal Student Aid FAFSA Web site OR Request a paper application from the Federal Student Aid Information Center at 800-4-FED-AID (800-433-3243) OR Print a paper application at Federal Student Aid . Southwestern Adventist University code: 003619 Step 3 Complete any other documentation requested by Student Financial Services needed for verification. Step 4 When all documents have been received and verified, your aid will be awarded and you will receive an Award Notification in the mail. You may also view your awards on your student portal. About Us Home Enrollment Academics Programs Finances Estimated Costs for 2013-2014 Financial Aid Student Accounts Tuition Price Calculator Department Staff Services Campus Life Support Us Music Festival Graduation News & Events Bulletin Information Southwestern Alerts Search Directory Map Tour FAQ Upcoming Events Front Page Events Calendar for Southwestern Adventist University ... Departmental Assembly (9/12/2013) 12/09 - 2013 09/12/2013 ... Departmental Vespers (10/11/2013) 11/10 - 2013 10/11/2013 ... University Experience (11/17/2013) 17/11 - 2013 11/17/2013 ... The Southwesterner The Southwesterner » Front Page ... University Bookstore Service Opens Tomorrow 10/07 - 2013 Front 